- op: discuss  # e047
  at: '2026-07-11T03:50:37Z'  # e047
  by: agent  # e047
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e047
  clock: 3  # e047
  nonce: e047  # e047
  message: "Fixed (PR merged as c31fea4459). Root cause: Limits.add_skipped_language (limits.py:140) had ZERO non-test callers (grep across packages/*/src -> only the definition + tests; verify_claims.py:491 even carried a 'dead field — WI-nihir' comment), so limits.skipped_languages was structurally always []; a language the profile DETECTED but for which no analyzer pass ran (tree-sitter grammar failed to load, unsupported language, or a crashed pass — the skipped branch routes to limits.skipped_passes and never appends an AnalysisRun) was silently absent from the honesty signal. Fix (structural, single chokepoint): new finalize._detected_unanalyzed_languages(ctx) computes detected = profile.languages keys - CONFIG_LANGUAGES, analyzed = union of the languages covered by the analyzer whose pass_id appears in analysis_runs (pass_id==RegisteredAnalyzer.name per all_analyzers.py:218; languages via the same 'set(languages) if languages else {name}' convention as all_analyzers.py:202), and _finalize_skipped_into_limits drains sorted(detected - analyzed) through the previously-dead setter before committing behavior_map['limits']. One site covers grammar-load-failure, missing-analyzer, and crashed-pass causes with no per-analyzer edit. No schema change (skipped_languages was already always-emitted; value [] -> populated). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: live 'hypergumbo run' on a synthetic python+Makefile repo now emits limits.skipped_languages == ['makefile'] (makefile detected in profile, no makefile analyzer — only linker/build-target passes) where it was [] before. Production-path tests in test_finalize.py: test_skipped_languages_populated_for_detected_unanalyzed_language (go detected, only python analyzed -> ['go']), _empty_when_all_detected_languages_analyzed ([]), _excludes_config_only_languages (json filtered, haskell flagged). 100% coverage. (declared-fields F2 keystone; siblings WI-muzus/WI-zusok analysis_depth + WI-togop not_captured tracked separately.)"  # e047
